coder › Implemented `wrap(text, width)` in `src/wrap.ts` and added tests in `src/wrap.test.ts`.

What changed
- `src/wrap.ts` — implemented wrapping:
  - Throws `RangeError` when `width < 1`.
  - Splits input into paragraphs on blank lines, keeps one blank line between them, and drops leading/trailing blank lines.
  - Collapses runs of whitespace within a paragraph to a single space.
  - Greedily wraps words onto lines of at most `width` characters, breaking at spaces.
  - Splits words longer than `width` into `width`-sized chunks.
- `src/wrap.test.ts` — 13 tests covering short text, space breaking, space-run collapsing, paragraph separation, long-word splitting, `width = 1`, empty text, and the `RangeError` cases.

Decisions I made that the plan didn't specify
- Whitespace-only lines (e.g. `"   "`) count as blank paragraph separators, and tabs/newlines within a paragraph are treated like spaces.
- Leading/trailing blank lines are dropped; consecutive blank lines collapse to one.
- When a word exceeds `width`, it first breaks at the preceding space (if a line is already started), then the word is split into `width`-sized chunks; the final chunk can share a line with following words if they fit.

